        "original_id": "18ced793-611d-5c1d-9db9-8fd9bb138c13",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Minardi M190, Minardi M189B, Cosworth DFR V8 engine, Pirelli tyres\n- Companies: Pirelli & C. S.p.A., ChemChina\n- People: Frank Gardner\n- Topics: Formula One, European F5000 Championship\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Gardner debuted in the Formula One World Championship on 11 July 1964 and later participated in nine World Championship Formula One Grands Prix.\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. was listed on the Milan Stock Exchange from 1922.\n- Frank Gardner was a European F5000 champion.\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. is a multinational company based in Milan, Italy.\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. is now an overseas subsidiary of the Chinese state-owned enterprise ChemChina.\n- The Minardi M189 was updated as the M189B for the season and was used for the first two races of the year before the Minardi M190 replaced it.\n- The Minardi M190 was powered by the Cosworth DFR V8 engine and ran on Pirelli tyres.",
